00:17:33.345 --> 00:17:36.225
put in an electronic permitting system

00:17:36.385 --> 00:17:44.930
because we're reducing the total time available and we're going to have to make ourselves more efficient if we're going to make this work without inconveniencing

00:17:44.930 --> 00:17:45.890
the public.

00:17:46.290 --> 00:17:50.930
And so we can talk about that a little bit later. I sent everybody on the commission

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:52.690
the contract

00:17:53.330 --> 00:17:56.130
or a proposed contract from Permit Link.

00:17:56.745 --> 00:17:59.545
So I have looked at a couple of vendors.

00:17:59.865 --> 00:18:04.745
You know there's really only two vendors that are commonly used in this area. Permit Link

00:18:04.825 --> 00:18:11.785
is the El Chipo one and there's a better vendor out there but it's more than double the cost

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:13.120
And

00:18:13.600 --> 00:18:17.280
there's a big initial startup cost for implementation,

00:18:17.760 --> 00:18:24.400
which Permit Link doesn't have. So my recommendation is we go with Permit Link that will accomplish what we need.

00:18:24.800 --> 00:18:26.960
And we're also going to turn around and just

00:18:27.275 --> 00:18:30.955
what permit link will do is allow us to just be billed

00:18:31.595 --> 00:18:33.755
per the number of permits pulled.

00:18:33.995 --> 00:18:37.835
And then we simply pay for it by tacking on a fee to each permit.

00:18:38.075 --> 00:18:41.675
And the other advantage is it'll allow people to pay electronically.

00:18:42.120 --> 00:18:43.800
So it's much faster

00:18:43.960 --> 00:18:53.640
on the part of an applicant and it's more convenient in the sense that they can be sitting on their Barco Lounger with a beer at 11:30 at night submitting their permit

00:18:53.880 --> 00:18:54.520
